    <div class="itdgl-clinic-intro">
      <p>Meta + Google + YouTube ads for a hair transplant clinic in Navi Mumbai, Maharashtra operate at high AOV (Rs 60,000-4 lakh per procedure) with 4-12 week consideration cycles + medical-tourism catchment. Higher CPL acceptable (Navi Mumbai: Rs 800-4,000 per qualified lead) because AOV justifies. This FAQ answers 12 questions Navi Mumbai hair transplant clinics ask about ads.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="itdgl-evidence-band">
      <strong>ITD CLINIC MARKETING &mdash; WHAT WE ACTUALLY DO:</strong>
      ITD GrowthLabs runs full-stack digital marketing for hair transplant + fue + fut clinics across Thane, Mumbai, Navi Mumbai, Dombivli, Kalyan, Nagpur, Nashik, and Pune. Social media management + Reels + viral content, Meta + Google ads, website + online booking + WhatsApp Cloud API integration, Google Business Profile optimisation + local SEO, and patient lead generation. We work with clinics that don't have in-house marketing teams — treating the marketing function as an outsourced growth partner, not a vendor. Every answer below reflects live clinic work.
    </div>

    <div class="itdgl-faq-list" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What channel mix for Meta + Google ads for a Navi Mumbai hair transplant clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Meta + Instagram + Reels 35-40%, Google Search + Ads 25-30% (high-intent 'hair transplant near me' + 'FUE cost' queries), YouTube + long-form ads 15-20% (buyers research extensively), WhatsApp CTWA 10-15% (inside-sales handoff), GMB local ads 8-12%. Medical-tourism campaigns for Tier 2/3 + international 10-15% of budget.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What CPL should we expect for hair transplant ads in Navi Mumbai?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">In Navi Mumbai: Rs 500-1,500 general hair-transplant inquiry, Rs 800-2,500 FUE/DHI-specific + graft-count-qualified, Rs 1,500-5,000 high-AOV bespoke consultation. Lead-to-booked-consultation 15-30% (lower than dermatology/trichology because higher-consideration). Cost per booked consultation Rs 3,000-15,000. Consultation-to-treatment 20-40%. Effective cost per acquired patient Rs 15,000-60,000. Justified by AOV Rs 60,000-4 lakh per procedure.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What is a realistic monthly ad budget for a Navi Mumbai hair transplant clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Rs 40,000-4 lakh. Starter Rs 50K-1.5L/month Navi Mumbai for solo Rs 10-30 lakh revenue. Growth Rs 1.5-5L for 2-3 surgeon Rs 30 lakh-1.5 crore. Enterprise Rs 5-15L for multi-location/destination clinic. Higher ad-spend absolute vs dermatology because higher AOV supports higher CPL. Rule 12-20% of procedure revenue during acquisition growth.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What creative formats work best for hair transplant paid ads?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Meta + Reels + YouTube: (1) Before-after 6-12 month growth compilation Reels (highest CTR + conversion), (2) FUE vs FUT vs DHI explainer video, (3) Surgeon-technique + operating room BTS, (4) Patient journey video milestone documentation, (5) Facility + team + technology tour, (6) Graft-count-calculator interactive ad. YouTube long-form 5-15 min patient documentation + surgeon interview + FAQ. Google Search + Shopping + Local Services Ads.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What compliance rules apply to hair transplant paid ads?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Cannot guarantee graft-yield or hair-density. Before-after with consent + disclaimer + timeline. Surgeon credentials verifiable. No comparative claims. Aggressive discount prohibited. Medical-tourism marketing to Tier 2/3 + international requires both-jurisdiction compliance. Meta + Google medical + surgery vertical policies apply. In Navi Mumbai, Maharashtra Medical Council + Maharashtra FDA + NMMC health department + surgical facility norms.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How does CAPI + attribution + inside-sales work for a Navi Mumbai hair transplant clinic?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Server-side CAPI + Enhanced Conversions + WhatsApp CTWA + offline conversion upload for phone/inside-sales/consultation-close (30-50% attribution loss without offline upload). Multi-touch attribution over 90-180 day consideration cycle. Inside-sales rep (dedicated) qualifies WhatsApp leads within 5-10 min business hours.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we handle attribution + LTV/CAC for hair transplant paid ads?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">CRM + multi-touch + long-cycle attribution + procedure revenue attribution + medical-tourism catchment split. 5-year LTV Rs 75K-5L per procedure patient + Rs 20K-1.2L maintenance. Payback 6-12 months.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How do we control ad fatigue for hair transplant paid ads?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Creative velocity 8-15 units/week Growth. Audience + creative refresh 4-6 weeks (hair-transplant buyer researches longer, less fatigued). Frequency cap 3-5/week. Exclude converted from prospecting. Long-form video + patient documentation content injection prevents fatigue naturally.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What are common paid-ads mistakes for Navi Mumbai hair transplant clinics?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">(1) First-consultation CPA vs procedure-revenue LTV bidding. (2) Missing offline conversion upload (30-50% attribution loss). (3) Weak multi-touch attribution. (4) No WhatsApp inside-sales flow (misses 30-50% high-AOV close). (5) Under-invested video creative. (6) Same creative + audience for local vs medical-tourism. (7) ASCI-violating graft-yield guarantee copy. (8) English-only in Navi Mumbai. (9) Aggressive discount marketing. (10) No YouTube long-form ads. (11) Weak landing pages + no facility/surgeon-credibility content. (12) No graft-count-calculator interactive experience.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What peak-season ad spend concentration for Navi Mumbai hair transplant?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Diwali + wedding season + Winter + Monsoon + Ganesh Chaturthi + Gudi Padwa. Wedding season Nov-Feb (grooms + brides book pre-wedding), summer + monsoon (increased hair-loss awareness). Concentration less extreme than fashion/dermatology (30-40% in peaks) because hair-transplant is year-round decision. Medical-tourism creates weekend + holiday-adjacent inquiry spikes.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">What KPIs to track weekly for hair transplant paid ads?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">CPL + cost per booked video-consultation + cost per in-person consultation + cost per procedure + graft-count-weighted revenue attribution + inside-sales conversion + WhatsApp response rate + medical-tourism catchment mix.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="itdgl-faq-item">
        <h2 class="itdgl-faq-q">How does ITD run Meta + Google + YouTube ads for Navi Mumbai hair transplant clinics?</h2>
        <div class="itdgl-faq-a">Full-stack: channel mix + video-heavy creative (8-15/week) + CAPI + offline conversion upload + LTV/CAC + WhatsApp inside-sales + landing-page CRO + medical-tourism campaigns + weekly review + monthly QBR. Compliance-safe creative + surgeon credibility + patient journey documentation. Bundled with full retainer (Rs 35,000-2.5 lakh) + transparent ad-spend.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

